# modelos.logi: an agent that looks after the language models of some machines. The scripts it needs are NOT here.
#   logi spec modelos.logi          the specification of each script it lacks (no model, nothing written)
#   logi program modelos.logi       a model writes them: validated, tried in a pretend world, anchored in programs/
#   logi try modelos.logi --program talk to it, now that it has its scripts
name: modelos
about: language models installed on machines

== 1. conversation
client: which models are on m1?
agent:  mistral is on m1
client: is llama3 on m1?
agent:  No: llama3 is not on m1
client: get llama3 installed on m1
agent:  Done: llama3 is installed on m1
client: is llama3 on m1?
agent:  Yes: llama3 is on m1

== 2. facts
installed(M, X) = {X} is installed on {M}      [set; program]

== 3. rules
model(X) = {X} is a model
model(llama3). model(mistral). model(qwen2).
here(M, X) = {X} is on {M} | which models are on {M}{X=?}
here(M, X) :- installed(M, X), model(X).

== 4. meta-interpreters
-- execute
act(installed(M, X), [install, M, X]).
-- program
observe installed(M, X)    via ollama           # LOOKS: M, X given = check, free = list
act install                via ollama           # the script behind act(...) above
rehearse m1: mistral qwen2                      # pretend machines to try them on
rehearse m2: qwen2
